{
 "lines": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start": 3.5,
   "end": 8.321,
   "text": "I ride the last bus home every night, all the way to the end of the line."
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start": 9.021,
   "end": 14.141,
   "text": "The driver, an old man named Ray, gave me one rule on my first ride."
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start": 14.841,
   "end": 21.156,
   "text": "If this bus ever stops at Hollow Street... keep your eyes down. And don't let anything sit next to you."
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start": 21.956,
   "end": 25.199,
   "text": "There is no Hollow Street. Not on any map."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start": 25.899,
   "end": 32.235,
   "text": "For a whole year, we never stopped there. Just rain, empty seats, and Ray humming to the radio."
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start": 33.035,
   "end": 37.387,
   "text": "Then, one night, the bus slowed down... between two black fields."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start": 37.987,
   "end": 41.528,
   "text": "The doors hissed open. Ray didn't say a word."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start": 42.528,
   "end": 47.861,
   "text": "I stared at my shoes. Slow, wet footsteps came up the steps... and down the aisle."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start": 49.861,
   "end": 52.421,
   "text": "They stopped right beside me."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start": 53.621,
   "end": 57.589,
   "text": "I put my bag on the empty seat. And I didn't breathe."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start": 58.789,
   "end": 63.163,
   "text": "After a long time, the footsteps turned... and went back to the front."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start": 63.963,
   "end": 70.619,
   "text": "As we pulled away, I saw Ray through the back window... standing in the rain at Hollow Street, waving goodbye."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start": 71.819,
   "end": 76.235,
   "text": "The driver never turned around. He just said, in Ray's voice..."
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start": 77.435,
   "end": 79.995,
   "text": "Don't worry. I know where you live."
  }
 ],
